<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil cuts posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil cuts posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said it lowered the price it would pay for some grades of crude oil by C$7.00/cubic metre or C$1.11/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Edmonton light sweet C$167.00/cubic metre, or C$26.55/barrel</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$155.00/cubic metre, or C$24.64/barrel</p>
<p>Bow River at Hardisty C$127.00/cubic metre, or C$20.19/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$138.00/cubic metre, or C$21.94/barrel</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
